  "configuration_id": "config_006",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_005 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) achieved 0.650 acc / 0.628 F1, a large jump over config_004 (same encoder, singleprofile: 0.520). This confirms multiprofile aggregation is a major design lever. Uncertainty: we do not yet know whether the aggregation method (avgpool vs. transformer) further improves performance, or whether avgpool is already near-optimal for this encoder. Question: config_006 changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding rna_only, multiprofile, and scvi_n200 fixed, giving a clean single-variable comparison against config_005. Why best next step: it directly exploits the strongest evidence (best-performing config) to isolate the effect of aggregation, a design choice that will propagate to every future multimodal experiment. If transformer substantially outperforms avgpool, we gain a better aggregation for all downstream fusion experiments; if it does not, we confirm avgpool suffices and can redirect budget toward encoder or modality questions. This is the highest-information, lowest-risk next experiment under the limited budget."
}

